<DocsLayout title="CLI reference" description="Complete command reference for the VulnWeave local CLI.">
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">REFERENCE</p><h1>CLI reference</h1><p class="lede">The compact commands are the normal way to use VulnWeave. They read the committed project policy where present. The advanced format options remain available for scripts and focused analysis.</p>
    <h2>Everyday commands</h2>
    <div class="command-grid"><code>init [path]</code><span>Create starter configuration, baseline, and Semgrep rule without overwriting existing files.</span><code>doctor</code><span>Show the VulnWeave version and installed analyzer versions. It does not scan.</span><code>scan [path]</code><span>Run configured analyzers and print a summary.</span><code>findings [path]</code><span>Show canonical findings in a table.</span><code>quality [path]</code><span>Show advisory maintainability signals.</span><code>priorities [path]</code><span>Rank findings using explicit local evidence.</span><code>report [path]</code><span>Print a self-contained HTML report to standard output.</span><code>history [path]</code><span>Show saved local scan trend.</span><code>review [path] --base &lt;ref&gt;</code><span>Create a changed-code review packet against a Git reference.</span><code>ci [path]</code><span>Run a summary gate and require selected analyzers to complete.</span></div>
    <h2>Useful output formats</h2><pre><code>pnpm cli -- . --format summary&#10;pnpm cli -- . --format table --severity high&#10;pnpm cli -- . --format priorities&#10;pnpm cli -- . --format graph&#10;pnpm cli -- . --format symbols&#10;pnpm cli -- . --format reachability&#10;pnpm cli -- . --format upgrades&#10;pnpm cli -- . --format remediation&#10;pnpm cli -- . --format ownership&#10;pnpm cli -- . --format trend --history 20&#10;pnpm cli -- . --format sarif &gt; vulnweave.sarif</code></pre>
    <h2>Filtering and analyzer selection</h2><pre><code>pnpm cli -- . --analyzer all --format table --severity high&#10;pnpm cli -- . --category dependency --format table&#10;pnpm cli -- . --filter-analyzer osv --format table&#10;pnpm cli -- . --analyzer semgrep --semgrep-config rules/semgrep-starter.yml</code></pre><p>Available analyzer selections are <code>all</code>, <code>gitleaks</code>, <code>semgrep</code>, <code>osv</code>, and <code>trivy</code>. An analyzer failure is recorded while other analyzers can still return results. Add <code>--require-analyzers</code> when a missing or failed selected analyzer must fail the run.</p>
    <h2>Saved scans and comparisons</h2><p>Runs are stored locally in <code>.vulnweave/runs/</code>; the latest is <code>.vulnweave/latest.json</code>. Use <code>--no-save</code> for an ephemeral run, <code>--compare latest</code> to display changes, and <code>--baseline latest</code> to gate only new findings relative to the last scan.</p>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
